$ ada: lagrange send @echo hello from CI --wait
You said: hello from CI
hello from CI
! completed (task <id1>)
[exit 0]

$ ada: lagrange send @bob Approve 200 hoodies for 2,800 EUR?
<id2>
! Sent to @bob. Check on it with: lagrange task <id2> --wait
[exit 0]

$ bob: lagrange waiting --mine
TASK                                  WAITING ON  ASKED BY  SINCE     QUESTION
<id2>  @bob (you)  @ada      just now  Approve 200 hoodies for 2,800 EUR?
[exit 0]

$ ada: lagrange task <id2> --wait
Go ahead.
! Waiting on @bob…
! completed, answered by @bob (task <id2>)
[exit 0]

$ ada: lagrange send @bob Ship the release?
<id3>
! Sent to @bob. Check on it with: lagrange task <id3> --wait
[exit 0]

$ bob: lagrange answer <id3> --reject Not on a Friday.
! Answered <id3>.
[exit 0]

$ ada: lagrange task <id3> --wait
Not on a Friday.
! rejected, answered by @bob (task <id3>)
! lagrange: the task was rejected
[exit 3]

$ ada: lagrange send @bob Lunch? --wait --timeout 1s
! Waiting on @bob…
! input-required, waiting on @bob (task <id4>)
! lagrange: still input-required; the task goes on. Wait again with: lagrange task <id4> --wait
[exit 4]

$ ada: lagrange send @ada Remember the milk --wait
! input-required, waiting on @ada (task <id5>)
! lagrange: the task asks you. Answer with: lagrange answer <id5> "…"
[exit 5]

$ ada: lagrange send @echo --data {"order":"PO-1","qty":200} --wait --json
{
  "taskId": "<id6>",
  "contextId": "<id7>",
  "state": "completed",
  "done": true,
  "text": "You said: {\"order\":\"PO-1\",\"qty\":200}\n{\"order\":\"PO-1\",\"qty\":200}"
}
[exit 0]

$ ada: lagrange send @nobody hi
! lagrange: no such address: @nobody
[exit 1]

$ bob: lagrange answer <id2> --approve
! lagrange: the task isn't waiting for an answer
[exit 1]

$ ada: lagrange runs --limit 3
RUN                                   STATE                  FROM → TO     UPDATED   TITLE
<id6>  completed              @ada → @echo  just now  {"order":"PO-1","qty":200}
<id5>  input-required (@ada)  @ada → @ada   just now  Remember the milk
<id4>  input-required (@bob)  @ada → @bob   just now  Lunch?
[exit 0]

$ ada: lagrange runs -q hoodies
RUN                                   STATE      FROM → TO    UPDATED   TITLE
<id2>  completed  @ada → @bob  just now  Approve 200 hoodies for 2,800 EUR?
[exit 0]

$ ada: lagrange run <id2>
Approve 200 hoodies for 2,800 EUR?
completed · @ada → @bob · 1 task · started just now
Outcome: Go ahead.

TASK                                  STATE              FROM → TO    SUMMARY
<id2>  completed by @bob  @ada → @bob  Approve 200 hoodies for 2,800 EUR?
[exit 0]

$ ada: lagrange run <id2> --overlap
AGENT  TOOL CALLS  COST
total  0           $0.00

No repeated tool calls.
[exit 0]

$ ada: lagrange run <id2> --knows --json
[]
[exit 0]

$ ada: lagrange waiting
TASK                                  WAITING ON  ASKED BY  SINCE     QUESTION
<id4>  @bob        @ada      just now  Lunch?
<id5>  @ada (you)  @ada      just now  Remember the milk
[exit 0]

